// The ABI-membership gate (#1662) — the Bit port of the deleted harness
// `rootabi_membership`.
//
// THE PROPERTY. Two halves must agree on one set of names: the half that EMITS a
// `call bit_rt_*` relocation, and the half that DEFINES the symbol. Every name
// the first can emit must be defined by the second, or it is an undefined symbol
// at link time — in every shipped binary that reaches the call, not just a test.
//
// WHY IT HAD TO MOVE. The deleted gate read the defining half from the native
// runtime's source (`export fn` plus `comptime { @export(...) }`) and asserted
// that set was a subset of the Bit pins. Right question while both runtimes
// existed, but it DIES WITH ITS OWN ORACLE: G3 deletes that source, and a
// membership floor against a directory with none of it left is a hard failure
// with nothing wrong — whose obvious "fix" is to delete the gate with the
// files, taking the property with it.
//
// WHERE IT POINTS NOW. The emitting half is the compiler's own RtFn table, which
// survives the deletion: `compiler/irrtfns.bit`'s `rtFnTags` through the symbol
// convention `compiler/codegen.bit`'s `rtSymbol` states (`bit_rt_<tag>`, except
// `err_set`/`err_get`, whose symbols read verb-first), plus the names a backend
// emits DIRECTLY rather than through an `rt_call` — `bit_rt_gc_alloc`,
// `bit_rt_iface_lookup`, `bit_rt_safepoint`. The providing half is unchanged:
// the `@symbol("bit_rt_*")` pins under `runtime/**/*.bit`. So is the direction —
// every emitted name needs a provider, while a pin with no caller is fine, since
// the port-internal `bit_rt_port_*` names were never in the ABI.
//
// THE TABLE IS NOT THE ONLY DEMAND SOURCE, deliberately: it is written by hand,
// so it can fall behind the compiler it describes. The compiler is scanned too —
// every `<var>.name = "<tag>"`
// whose `<var>` came from `mkInstr(Op.RtCall, ...)`, and every tag
// `compiler/lowerprim.bit`'s `primRtName` returns. That half is INCOMPLETE by
// construction (a tag reaching `.name` through a variable, as `print`/`eprint`
// do, is invisible to a text scanner), and the floors are what stop the
// incompleteness from passing quietly.
//
// It also runs the other way, which is what keeps a HAND-WRITTEN table honest:
// every `rt_call` name the compiler is actually seen to build must appear in
// `rtFnTags`. A floor only catches the table shrinking; `checkTableCovers`
// catches the compiler growing past it, which is the likelier direction and the
// one that ends in an undefined symbol at link time.
//
// THE FLOORS, and why they are right after the deletion. PER-SOURCE, for the
// reason `_tests_/bit/pollfree.bit` records: one total floor lets one oracle die
// while another's growth keeps the sum up.
//
//   `minRtFnTags` 90 against today's 96 — the same 96 the seed's enum carried
//   when it was deleted, copied whole rather than re-derived. The deleted
//   gate's 90-against-103 was the same shape and too slack — it would have
//   absorbed the loss of thirteen
//   symbols in silence. 90 leaves room to retire a primitive or two (the
//   compiler already lowers `sqrt`/`floor`/`float_bits` as IR ops, so the table
//   shrinking is real) and no room for the table moving, being renamed, or the
//   block parser failing to find it.
//
//   `minCompilerTags` 80 against today's 84, same argument for the Bit-side scan.
//   `minDemand` 96 against today's 99 — the union, so it cannot go vacuous even
//   if both per-source scans clear their own floors on garbage.
//   `minPins` 250 against today's 306 (the deleted gate used 200 against 277): the
//   population has only grown as the port completed, and a broken pin scan
//   yields ~0, not 240.
//
// IF `compiler/irrtfns.bit` GOES this gate FAILS LOUDLY, and so it should: the
// compiler scan alone cannot meet `minRtFnTags` (84 < 90), because it is
// incomplete by construction. That is the design, not an oversight — the
// alternative to a red gate is a green one that proves nothing. Do not answer it
// with a lower floor. This is how it behaved when the deleted seed compiler's
// `ir` module was the oracle and #1593 deleted it (#1858); the property moved
// with the table.
//
// THE TWO WAYS A TEXT SCANNER GOES WRONG, both carried over from the deleted
// gate's header because both actually happened, and both unit-tested in
// `checkScanners` before the walk runs:
//
//   (1) A FALSE POSITIVE IS NOT NOISE. The deleted native runtime's `root`
//       module held `fatal("bit_rt_string_from_float: float text exceeds
//       buffer")`, and the
//       rule "any `bit_rt_*` literal is an export name" reported it as a missing
//       provider. An unsatisfiable demand is what pushes someone to weaken the
//       check. So a literal counts only when the WHOLE literal is one identifier
//       (never `"bit_rt_x: ..."`, never an interpolation), only outside comments,
//       and — for `.name =` — only off an `Op.RtCall` local. `atoms.name =
//       "bit_stack_maps"` is the live trap on that last rule.
//
//   (2) A FALSE NEGATIVE IS A GREEN HOLE. The deleted gate was got wrong by hand
//       twice, green both times: reading only `export fn` (missing
//       `bit_rt_safepoint`), then only the `root` module (missing `bit_rt_unmap_pages`).
//       The same class here is a pin the scanner fails to see, so a `@symbol(...)`
//       not attached to a `function` on its own or the next line is a HARD
//       FAILURE, not a skip.
//
// `compiler/*check.bit` is excluded from the emitting scan: those are the
// compiler's in-tree unit tests, whose fixtures name symbols no runtime defines
// on purpose (`bit_rt_absent`, `bit_rt_probe`, `bit_rt_no_such_symbol_exists_anywhere`).
// What that exclusion could hide is a real emit site, so the five directly
// emitted names are asserted BY NAME as anchors.
//
// Usage (cwd is the repository root):
//
//     bit run _tests_/bit/abimembers
//
// `BIT_REPO` overrides the repository root (default "."), which is also how this
// gate is mutation-tested: copy the tree, break one pin, point `BIT_REPO` at it.
//
// #2867 phase 2 split this file into `_tests_/bit/abimembers/{abimembers,scanners}.bit`:
// the three source-text scanners and their own unit tests now live in the
// sibling `scanners.bit`, no `import`, one shared scope. This file dropped
// from 917 to 355 lines and kept the walk over real files, the demand-set
// gate, the floors, and `main`.

import { exists, isDir, readFile, walk } from "std/fs"
import { exit, envOr } from "std/os"
import { hasSuffix } from "std/strings"

// ==== Bounds — every walk and every scan is provably finite (Power of 10 rule 2). ====

// Mirrors `rootabi_shared.max_bit_files`: an order of magnitude above today's
// count of runtime and compiler sources.
const maxBitFiles: int = 1024
// Mirrors `rootabi_shared.max_source_bytes` (1 << 22).
const maxSourceBytes: int = 4194304
const maxLinesPerFile: int = 200000

const abiPrefix: string = "bit_rt_"

// ==== The floors — see this file's header for why each number is what it is. ====

const minRtFnTags: int = 90
const minCompilerTags: int = 80
const minDemand: int = 96
const minPins: int = 250

// #3984: `tools/build/abiarity.bit`'s hand-written `directEmissionSymbols()`
// table has the identical flat shape as `rtFnTags` above, so `scanFlatStringTable`
// (`scanners.bit`) reads it the same way under a different header.
const directEmissionHeaderNew: string = "fn directEmissionSymbols(): []string {"
const directEmissionHeaderOld: string = "function directEmissionSymbols(): []string {"

// The lexical helpers and the three scanners (RtFn table, compiler rt_call/
// direct-emission, runtime pins), plus their own unit tests, now live in the
// sibling `scanners.bit` (#2867 phase 2) — this file calls `rtSymbol`,
// `scanRtFnTags`, `scanPins`, `scanCompilerFile` and `checkScanners` from
// there via the shared scope.

// ==== The walk ====

class Sources {
  paths: []string,
  ok: bool,
}

// Every `.bit` file under `dir`, bounded.
fn bitSources(dir: string): Sources {
  let out = Sources{ paths: []string(0), ok: false }
  if (!isDir(dir)) {
    eprint("abimembers: ${dir} is not a directory (set BIT_REPO to the repository root)\n")
    return out
  }
  let paths = walk(dir) catch e {
    eprint("abimembers: cannot walk ${dir}: ${e.message()}\n")
    return out
  }
  for p of paths {
    if (!hasSuffix(p, ".bit")) {
      continue
    }
    out.paths = append(out.paths, p)
    if (len(out.paths) > maxBitFiles) {
      eprint("abimembers: more than ${maxBitFiles} sources under ${dir}; raise the bound deliberately\n")
      return out
    }
  }
  out.ok = true
  return out
}

fn readBounded(path: string): string {
  let source = readFile(path) catch e {
    eprint("abimembers: cannot read ${path}: ${e.message()}\n")
    return ""
  }
  if (len(source) > maxSourceBytes) {
    eprint("abimembers: ${path} is larger than ${maxSourceBytes} bytes\n")
    return ""
  }
  return source
}

// The providing half.
fn collectPins(repo: string): PinScan {
  let out = PinScan{ names: []string(0), bad: 0 }
  let src = bitSources("${repo}/runtime")
  if (!src.ok) {
    out.bad = out.bad + 1
    return out
  }
  for p of src.paths {
    let s = scanPins(readBounded(p))
    out.bad = out.bad + s.bad
    if (s.bad != 0) {
      eprint(
          "abimembers: ${p}: ${s.bad} `@symbol(\"bit_rt_*\")` pin(s) not attached to a " +
          "`function`. Teach `scanPins` about the shape — an unread pin is a provider this " +
          "gate cannot see.\n",
      )
    }
    for n of s.names {
      out.names = append(out.names, n)
    }
  }
  return out
}

// The emitting half, self-hosted side. `*check.bit` is excluded: see the header.
fn collectCompiler(repo: string): EmitScan {
  let out = EmitScan{ tags: []string(0), names: []string(0) }
  let src = bitSources("${repo}/compiler")
  if (!src.ok) {
    return out
  }
  for p of src.paths {
    if (hasSuffix(p, "check.bit")) {
      continue
    }
    scanCompilerFile(out, readBounded(p))
  }
  return out
}

// ==== The gate ====

class Demand {
  name: string,
  origin: string,
}

// The emitted names, deduplicated, each keeping the source that demanded it.
class DemandSet {
  items: []Demand,
  seen: map<string, bool>,
}

fn addDemand(d: DemandSet, name: string, origin: string) {
  if (len(name) == 0 || d.seen[name]) {
    return
  }
  d.seen[name] = true
  d.items = append(d.items, Demand{ name: name, origin: origin })
}

fn demandFromTags(d: DemandSet, tags: []string, origin: string) {
  for t of tags {
    addDemand(d, rtSymbol(t), origin)
  }
}

// The five names the backends emit directly rather than through the RtFn table.
// Asserted BY NAME because they are what the `*check.bit` exclusion could hide,
// and because `bit_rt_set_err`/`bit_rt_get_err` exist only through `rtSymbol`'s
// special case — finding them proves this file's copy of that mapping is current.
fn emissionAnchors(): []string {
  return [
    "bit_rt_gc_alloc", "bit_rt_iface_lookup", "bit_rt_safepoint",
    "bit_rt_set_err", "bit_rt_get_err",
  ]
}

fn checkAnchors(names: []string): int {
  let have = map<string, bool>{}
  for n of names {
    have[n] = true
  }
  let missing = 0
  for a of emissionAnchors() {
    if (have[a]) {
      continue
    }
    eprint(
        "abimembers: `${a}` is emitted by no compiler source this gate can see. " +
        "A backend call site or `rtSymbol`/`safepointSymbol` moved, or it now lives in a " +
        "`*check.bit` file this scan skips — the demand set is no longer complete.\n",
    )
    missing = missing + 1
  }
  return missing
}

// How many DISTINCT names `xs` holds. Every floor counts distinct names, the way
// the deleted gate's hash-map `count()` did: a scan that reads one file twice must
// not be able to clear a floor with the duplicates.
fn distinct(xs: []string): int {
  let seen = map<string, bool>{}
  let n = 0
  for x of xs {
    if (seen[x]) {
      continue
    }
    seen[x] = true
    n = n + 1
  }
  return n
}

fn checkFloor(got: int, want: int, what: string): int {
  if (got >= want) {
    return 0
  }
  eprint(
      "abimembers: found only ${got} ${what} (expected at least ${want}). " +
      "The membership check is reading nothing useful there — see this file's header " +
      "on the floors; do NOT answer this by lowering one.\n",
  )
  return 1
}

fn reportMissing(demand: []Demand, pins: []string): int {
  let provided = map<string, bool>{}
  for p of pins {
    provided[p] = true
  }
  let missing = 0
  for d of demand {
    if (provided[d.name]) {
      continue
    }
    eprint(
        "abimembers: `${d.name}` is emitted by the compiler (${d.origin}) but NO " +
        "`@symbol(\"${d.name}\")` pin under runtime/ provides it. That is an undefined " +
        "symbol at link time in every binary reaching the call. Add the pinned Bit " +
        "provider, or drop the primitive from the compiler.\n",
    )
    missing = missing + 1
  }
  return missing
}

// #3984: cross-checks `tools/build/abiarity.bit`'s hand-written
// `directEmissionSymbols()` against what `deriveDirectEmissionSet` (scanners.bit)
// derives from `comp.names`/`table.tags` — see that file's header for the
// derivation. Split out of `main` to keep both under the complexity-10 ceiling
// (spec/LINT.md:186, E0204).
fn checkAbiarityDirectEmission(repo: string, comp: EmitScan, table: TagScan): int {
  let path = "${repo}/tools/build/abiarity.bit"
  if (!exists(path)) {
    eprint(
        "abimembers: ${path} is gone. It is where directEmissionSymbols() lives — " +
        "the hand-written list this check cross-references — so there is nothing " +
        "to compare against.\n",
    )
    return 1
  }
  let hand = scanFlatStringTable(
    readBounded(path),
    directEmissionHeaderNew,
    directEmissionHeaderOld,
  )
  let bad = hand.bad
  if (hand.bad != 0) {
    eprint(
        "abimembers: ${hand.bad} line(s) of tools/build/abiarity.bit's " +
        "directEmissionSymbols() are in a shape this gate does not understand.\n",
    )
  }
  let derived = deriveDirectEmissionSet(comp.names, table.tags)
  return bad + checkDirectEmissionList(derived, hand.tags)
}

fn main() {
  if (!checkScanners()) {
    eprint("FAIL abimembers: the source scanners do not pass their own unit tests\n")
    exit(1)
  }
  let repo = envOr("BIT_REPO", ".")
  let irPath = "${repo}/compiler/irrtfns.bit"
  if (!exists(irPath)) {
    eprint(
        "FAIL abimembers: ${irPath} is gone. Its `rtFnTags` table is this gate's " +
        "demand oracle — the canonical list of runtime primitives the compiler can call. " +
        "Restore it; a gate with no demand set passes everything.\n",
    )
    exit(1)
  }

  let table = scanRtFnTags(readBounded(irPath))
  let comp = collectCompiler(repo)
  let pins = collectPins(repo)

  let bad = table.bad
  if (table.bad != 0) {
    eprint(
        "abimembers: ${table.bad} line(s) of the `rtFnTags` table are in a shape this " +
        "gate does not understand; every one of them is a primitive it is not demanding.\n",
    )
  }
  bad = bad + pins.bad
  let nTags = distinct(table.tags)
  let nComp = distinct(comp.tags)
  let nPins = distinct(pins.names)
  bad = bad + checkFloor(nTags, minRtFnTags, "`rtFnTags` entries in compiler/irrtfns.bit")
  bad = bad + checkFloor(nComp, minCompilerTags, "`rt_call` names in compiler/*.bit")
  bad = bad + checkFloor(nPins, minPins, "`@symbol(\"bit_rt_*\")` pins under runtime/")
  bad = bad + checkAnchors(comp.names)
  bad = bad + checkTableCovers(table.tags, comp.tags)
  bad = bad + checkAbiarityDirectEmission(repo, comp, table)

  let demand = DemandSet{ items: []Demand(0), seen: map<string, bool>{} }
  demandFromTags(demand, table.tags, "compiler/irrtfns.bit rtFnTags")
  demandFromTags(demand, comp.tags, "compiler/*.bit rt_call")
  for n of comp.names {
    addDemand(demand, n, "compiler/*.bit direct emission")
  }
  bad = bad +
    checkFloor(len(demand.items), minDemand, "distinct `bit_rt_*` names the compiler emits")
  bad = bad + reportMissing(demand.items, pins.names)

  if (bad != 0) {
    eprint(
        "FAIL abimembers: ${bad} problem(s). Every `bit_rt_*` name the compiler emits " +
        "must be defined by a `@symbol` pin under runtime/ — that set is the ABI, and a " +
        "hole in it is an undefined symbol in every shipped binary.\n",
    )
    exit(1)
  }
  println(
      "PASS abimembers: ${len(demand.items)} `bit_rt_*` names the compiler emits " +
      "(${nTags} RtFn tags, ${nComp} compiler rt_call names) are all provided by the " +
      "${nPins} `@symbol` pins under runtime/",
  )
}
